1
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:43,930
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,130 --> 00:01:46,880
[Episode 21]

3
00:01:50,039 --> 00:01:50,840
President Li.

4
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:52,950
This time,

5
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,509
besides official business,

6
00:01:54,509 --> 00:01:56,509
I have a personal favor to ask of you.

7
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:58,539
Come here for a second.

8
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:01,640
This is the youngest

9
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:04,000
and most hardworking doctor

10
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,640
in our hospital,

11
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:06,590
Dr. Che.

12
00:02:06,590 --> 00:02:07,280
Hello.

13
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:07,950
Hello, President.

14
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:09,030
Let me offer you a toast.

15
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:09,800
Okay.

16
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:11,570
She wants to get a Ph.D.

17
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:14,390
We'll count on you for
her recommendation letter.

18
00:02:14,590 --> 00:02:15,360
No problem.

19
00:02:15,590 --> 00:02:16,960
We'll be family soon.

20
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,120
That's a different matter.

21
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,360
Whether we'll be family or not,

22
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,400
we don't know yet.

23
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:23,030
But you have promised her this.

24
00:02:23,030 --> 00:02:24,160
I'll be the witness.

25
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:26,360
Long,

26
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,560
why are you so sneaky?

27
00:02:33,030 --> 00:02:34,160
Long, what's wrong?

28
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,880
Something happened at home.

29
00:02:39,590 --> 00:02:43,750
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

30
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,280
All staff members,

31
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:44,680
-please report to the outpatient hall on the first floor.
-Have you seen Chen Junnan?

32
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:46,220
[No smoking] [Keep quiet]

33
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:46,030
Didn't he ask for leave?

34
00:02:46,030 --> 00:02:46,960
No.

35
00:02:47,310 --> 00:02:49,150
He was supposed to come this afternoon

36
00:02:49,150 --> 00:02:50,430
to attend the inquiry by

37
00:02:50,430 --> 00:02:51,710
the Medical Association's
Investigation Team.

38
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:52,710
He's not answering his phone

39
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:53,710
or replying to his messages.

40
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:54,680
What's going on?

41
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:57,370
Based on what I know about him,

42
00:02:57,430 --> 00:02:58,870
he's probably hiding.

43
00:02:59,430 --> 00:03:00,240
Hiding?

44
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:00,840
No.

45
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:02,430
How could he possibly avoid
something this big?

46
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:02,760
[Immunology Laboratory]

47
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:07,450
[Biochemistry Laboratory]
[Laboratory]

48
00:03:02,910 --> 00:03:04,080
He probably found a quiet place

49
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,360
to think things through.

50
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,190
Otherwise, he won't be able to get over it

51
00:03:06,190 --> 00:03:07,520
for the rest of his life.

52
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,030
This won't do.

53
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:10,190
We have to find him

54
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,250
and bring him here.

55
00:03:12,430 --> 00:03:13,430
How do we find him?

56
00:03:13,430 --> 00:03:15,030
It's like looking for
a needle in a haystack.

57
00:03:15,030 --> 00:03:15,680
Right.

58
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:16,280
In such a situation,

59
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:20,940
[Blood Test Department]

60
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:19,010
not even the police station
will accept the case.

61
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:20,590
Wait.

62
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:22,079
He's your best friend.

63
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:23,610
[Security Room]

64
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,710
Aren't you afraid something
might happen to him?

65
00:03:23,710 --> 00:03:24,910
What's the use of being afraid?

66
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:26,840
He has to rely on himself for many things.

67
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,280
Can you stay by his side 24 hours a day

68
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,150
for the rest of his life?

69
00:03:35,870 --> 00:03:36,870
Nonsense.

70
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:38,360
You know Secretary Lyu, right?

71
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:40,290
He's with the president every day.

72
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:49,090
Hello, President.

73
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,360
-President Long.
-President Long.

74
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:57,560
Dear colleagues,

75
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:00,750
in the past period of time,

76
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,840
you must have heard a lot of

77
00:04:03,430 --> 00:04:04,520
various rumors.

78
00:04:06,430 --> 00:04:09,230
Like how Xiaoximen Hospital
can't make ends meet,

79
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:14,680
how the higher-ups are
putting pressure on us,

80
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:17,209
and how Xiaoximen Hospital
is going to close.

81
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:18,920
I'm here

82
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,430
to tell you clearly that

83
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:22,190
they are all true.

84
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,190
No way, President Long.

85
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:27,240
Are we doomed?

86
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,040
You're kidding, right?

87
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:28,870
Director Long.

88
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:30,930
W-We can't just close down like this.

89
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:32,000
Right?

90
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,000
You're kidding, right?

91
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,460
We're such a big hospital.

92
00:04:37,950 --> 00:04:38,950
I hereby announce

93
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,250
that Xiaoximen Hospital will officially

94
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:45,600
begin liquidation proceedings today.

95
00:04:47,190 --> 00:04:48,790
As for what the future holds,

96
00:04:49,159 --> 00:04:51,159
what will happen to your positions,

97
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:54,400
and how compensation will be settled—

98
00:04:55,310 --> 00:04:58,020
everyone should just go home and
wait for further notice.

99
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:03,530
[Life lies in exercise.
Health lies in prevention.]

100
00:05:11,750 --> 00:05:12,950
You look pretty calm.

101
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:15,800
If I can pursue a Ph.D.,

102
00:05:15,870 --> 00:05:18,070
I would have to leave for a while anyway.

103
00:05:19,430 --> 00:05:20,830
Huang is the amazing one.

104
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:23,530
He has the longest tenure in
our department.

105
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,950
If the hospital closes,

106
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:26,390
he suffers the biggest loss.

107
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:27,190
Look at him.

108
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:28,630
Steady as a rock.

109
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:30,120
Long!

110
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:31,800
L-Long!

111
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,720
Long.

112
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:34,600
Didn't he say...

113
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,390
Didn't he say he has a way?

114
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:35,720
Where is he?

115
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,480
Left, left, left.

116
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,000
Long!

117
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,720
Left!

118
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,840
Don't you have a solution, Long?

119
00:05:41,370 --> 00:05:45,230
[Emergency Unit]

120
00:05:43,630 --> 00:05:44,430
Ma'am.

121
00:05:45,159 --> 00:05:45,950
Ma'am!

122
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,159
Ma'am.

123
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,720
Please, have mercy on me.

124
00:05:51,330 --> 00:05:53,790
[Boiler Room]

125
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,480
Ma'am!

126
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,510
Ma'am!

127
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:54,630
[Emergency Room]

128
00:05:54,990 --> 00:05:56,120
[Emergency Room]

129
00:05:55,159 --> 00:05:57,070
I beg you to have mercy.

130
00:05:57,680 --> 00:06:00,000
Please let my Xu Ling off the hook.

131
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:00,800
Ma'am!

132
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:03,920
Please let her go.

133
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:07,440
[Emergency Room]

134
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:05,240
The hospital is closed.

135
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,770
They still aren't leaving?

136
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:09,800
The compensation probably
hasn't been settled.

137
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:11,860
Is the one kneeling Xu Ling's father?

138
00:06:12,190 --> 00:06:14,070
Didn't they say all the inpatients

139
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:15,750
were transferred to Second Hospital?

140
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,810
It seems only his family hasn't left.

141
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,460
Thanks for your hard work.

142
00:06:27,870 --> 00:06:28,680
Dr. Zhong,

143
00:06:28,950 --> 00:06:30,560
you haven't gotten off work yet?

144
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,360
Our patient hasn't left yet.

145
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,360
How can we leave?

146
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:34,510
I have to see my duty through
to the very end.

147
00:06:34,510 --> 00:06:35,640
Come, hold on tight.

148
00:06:47,310 --> 00:06:50,110
Does changing the dressing
really hurt that much?

149
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,159
It's not the pain.

150
00:06:53,190 --> 00:06:54,790
I don't want to live anymore.

151
00:06:57,390 --> 00:06:59,190
Are you crying because of guilt,

152
00:06:59,310 --> 00:07:01,170
or are you afraid of going to jail?

153
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:03,480
Both.

154
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:13,650
Do you regret it?

155
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:19,150
You're only 19 years old.

156
00:07:19,630 --> 00:07:20,750
If the law doesn't require you to

157
00:07:20,750 --> 00:07:22,480
pay with your life for a life taken,

158
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:23,360
never say anything

159
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:24,600
about not wanting to live.

160
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,870
Easy for you to say.

161
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,520
You're not the one going to jail.

162
00:07:33,310 --> 00:07:34,270
I have a friend.

163
00:07:35,390 --> 00:07:37,560
He's about your age.

164
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,340
If he could trade places with you,

165
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,800
he would probably be very happy.

166
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:46,480
Why?

167
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,050
Did he kill someone too?

168
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,620
He didn't kill anyone,

169
00:07:52,270 --> 00:07:53,390
but he's very sick.

170
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:55,200
Time is running out.

171
00:07:57,190 --> 00:07:58,520
He once said something.

172
00:08:00,430 --> 00:08:02,960
He said you only have choices
if you're alive.

173
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:06,050
Now, I'm passing these words on to you.

174
00:08:07,190 --> 00:08:08,800
If you feel guilty,

175
00:08:09,510 --> 00:08:11,160
then live on with that guilt.

176
00:08:12,190 --> 00:08:13,510
If you don't care,

177
00:08:14,390 --> 00:08:15,360
then at least...

178
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:19,010
at least live on with the lessons learned.

179
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:23,000
Staying alive is the most important thing.

180
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,000
May I know...

181
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:32,960
which company is taking over
Xiaoximen Hospital?

182
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,000
Not for now.

183
00:08:34,669 --> 00:08:36,929
We are in contact with multiple parties.

184
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:39,030
We won't come to a decision so soon.

185
00:08:39,030 --> 00:08:40,600
So many companies

186
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:42,320
are interested in Xiaoximen.

187
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:43,960
Doesn't this show

188
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,550
the value of our hospital?

189
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:48,930
President Long.

190
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:51,870
For us ordinary people,

191
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:52,840
and I mean

192
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,550
for the vast majority of ordinary people,

193
00:08:54,550 --> 00:08:55,750
if they get sick,

194
00:08:56,030 --> 00:08:57,000
where is the first place they
would consider

195
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,080
to go for medical treatment?

196
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,210
A Grade 3A hospital.

197
00:09:00,390 --> 00:09:02,120
But there are also challenges.

198
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,120
Come on.

199
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,520
How much cheaper can you be than others?

200
00:09:06,670 --> 00:09:07,390
Besides,

201
00:09:07,390 --> 00:09:08,720
who will bear the losses

202
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:09,790
you caused?

203
00:09:09,790 --> 00:09:12,250
At least I didn't let
the government bear it.

204
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,560
Haven't you checked?

205
00:09:14,910 --> 00:09:15,720
The government's funding

206
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,870
is less than

207
00:09:16,870 --> 00:09:18,270
10% of our total revenue.

208
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:21,790
Long.

209
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:24,200
I know you are very capable.

210
00:09:24,670 --> 00:09:25,670
If you hadn't used those

211
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:27,390
messy methods to drag it out,

212
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:29,750
this Xiaoximen Hospital
would have closed down long ago.

213
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,510
The timing of this accident

214
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,520
is too coincidental.

215
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:35,200
This is God's will.

216
00:09:35,270 --> 00:09:36,360
What a load of crap.

217
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:39,070
If God makes people sick,

218
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:41,650
wouldn't you try to go against God's will?

219
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:43,030
Aren't you tired?

220
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:45,630
Come in.

221
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,360
President.

222
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,130
President Long.

223
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,800
I guessed you two would come.

224
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,030
Yes, this...

225
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:58,130
Sorry for all the trouble.

226
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,550
Please don't bother, President Long.

227
00:10:02,550 --> 00:10:03,200
It's hot.

228
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,390
Well...

229
00:10:13,030 --> 00:10:14,090
About this matter,

230
00:10:16,270 --> 00:10:18,030
I have to say what needs to be said.

231
00:10:18,030 --> 00:10:18,670
Yes.

232
00:10:22,150 --> 00:10:23,960
The estimated fine is

233
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,650
between 800,000 and 900,000 yuan.

234
00:10:29,630 --> 00:10:30,240
Well...

235
00:10:33,150 --> 00:10:33,960
Well...

236
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:36,080
Junnan sent me a message.

237
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:37,600
He says...

238
00:10:38,670 --> 00:10:41,270
He is willing to use his savings
over the years,

239
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:42,390
and the money my wife and I

240
00:10:42,390 --> 00:10:44,320
were going to use to buy him a house,

241
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:45,670
to...

242
00:10:46,670 --> 00:10:48,670
to give it to the patient's family.

243
00:10:49,390 --> 00:10:50,200
We...

244
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:53,030
He is too impulsive.

245
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:53,750
Yes.

246
00:10:57,270 --> 00:10:58,360
Actually,

247
00:10:58,790 --> 00:10:59,630
it cannot be determined

248
00:10:59,630 --> 00:11:02,030
that Chen Junnan acted intentionally

249
00:11:04,790 --> 00:11:06,440
or with negligence.

250
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,720
He definitely didn't do it on purpose.

251
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:08,440
President.

252
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:12,240
The hospital's insurance will pay.

253
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,600
T-Then...

254
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:16,070
Whatever the punishment is,

255
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:18,200
if it's our responsibility,

256
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,360
our family will bear it.

257
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:20,550
I-It's just that right now...

258
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:21,390
W-We...

259
00:11:29,150 --> 00:11:30,390
The personal fine will be 50,000 yuan.

260
00:11:30,390 --> 00:11:31,440
While the finance staff is still here,

261
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,870
go pay the money quickly.

262
00:11:33,510 --> 00:11:34,240
Brother.

263
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:35,170
President Long.

264
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,970
-Thank you, brother. I...
-Thank you so much.

265
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,120
I...

266
00:11:40,910 --> 00:11:41,630
Hubby.

267
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:43,470
Let's hurry and go pay the money.

268
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:44,790
Thank you.

269
00:11:44,790 --> 00:11:46,390
Hurry up, Hubby. Hurry.

270
00:12:08,730 --> 00:12:10,840
[Xiaoximen Hospital] [Name: Che Mingming]

271
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:39,630
Mingming,

272
00:12:41,390 --> 00:12:42,320
I've learned it.

273
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:42,870
I finally know

274
00:12:42,870 --> 00:12:44,000
how to open this door.

275
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:44,630
Look.

276
00:12:52,670 --> 00:12:53,670
Congratulations!

277
00:12:53,670 --> 00:12:55,730
You finally made it through the door.

278
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:58,080
Unfortunately,

279
00:12:59,630 --> 00:13:01,030
there's no door anymore.

280
00:13:09,450 --> 00:13:11,520
[Guanghua Road] [Dongdaqiao Road]

281
00:13:11,630 --> 00:13:13,050
[Our ultimate goal is to ensure
a stress-free move for our customers.]

282
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:12,910
As for you,

283
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,670
for violating company rules

284
00:13:14,670 --> 00:13:15,720
and fighting,

285
00:13:16,150 --> 00:13:17,950
we have no choice but to fire you.

286
00:13:18,910 --> 00:13:24,080
[Beijing Chengyi Moving Company]

287
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,000
How can this be considered

288
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:20,910
fighting?

289
00:13:21,510 --> 00:13:22,360
I was helping someone.

290
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:22,960
Someone was getting beaten up,

291
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,890
so I went over to do the right thing.

292
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,480
Stop fighting!

293
00:13:31,630 --> 00:13:32,840
You even got support, huh?

294
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:33,390
What?

295
00:13:33,390 --> 00:13:34,600
I am not support!

296
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:35,790
Don't even think about it.

297
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:36,600
I was just passing by!

298
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:37,870
I was beaten up like this.

299
00:13:37,870 --> 00:13:39,240
I couldn't just stand there.

300
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:40,240
It was self-defense.

301
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:41,480
I don't have time

302
00:13:41,870 --> 00:13:43,870
to investigate what you mentioned.

303
00:13:44,150 --> 00:13:45,320
By 4 p.m. today,

304
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:46,250
pack your things

305
00:13:46,510 --> 00:13:48,510
and move out of the staff dormitory.

306
00:13:49,830 --> 00:13:51,390
[Beijing Bank]

307
00:14:05,130 --> 00:14:05,400
[Calls]

308
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:10,810
[Contact]

309
00:14:10,830 --> 00:14:12,000
[Liu Zhengguang]

310
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,270
Work starts at 8 p.m.

311
00:14:32,270 --> 00:14:33,720
until 8 a.m. the next day.

312
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,480
Our unit doesn't attract thieves.

313
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:37,670
If there's nothing to do,
you can nap on the bed.

314
00:14:37,670 --> 00:14:38,720
But when the driver comes back,

315
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:39,910
he might knock on the window,

316
00:14:39,910 --> 00:14:41,600
and you have to help move people.

317
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,320
Do you understand what I mean?

318
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,120
I understand.

319
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,000
Then come in.

320
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,960
Zhao will come to take over

321
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:50,600
your shift tomorrow morning.

322
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:51,600
You two will share

323
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,720
daily necessities and what not.

324
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:53,600
If you're cold,

325
00:14:53,790 --> 00:14:55,080
there's an electric stove

326
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:56,480
and an electric blanket.

327
00:14:56,510 --> 00:14:57,720
Be very careful.

328
00:14:57,790 --> 00:14:59,250
Don't exceed 2,000 watts.

329
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:00,270
In this room,

330
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,270
the wires are thin

331
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:02,390
and easily short-circuit.

332
00:15:02,390 --> 00:15:04,200
Anyway, if anything happens,

333
00:15:04,390 --> 00:15:05,590
come find me anytime.

334
00:15:05,670 --> 00:15:06,630
Zhengguang's friend

335
00:15:06,630 --> 00:15:07,720
is my friend.

336
00:15:08,750 --> 00:15:09,880
Thank you, brother.

337
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:12,530
President Long,

338
00:15:12,790 --> 00:15:14,520
many old neighbors came today.

339
00:15:14,790 --> 00:15:17,250
Some have been standing here
since morning,

340
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:19,880
and some even rushed back
from out of town.

341
00:15:20,030 --> 00:15:23,120
Xiaoximen Hospital has stood on
this street for so many years.

342
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:24,850
How many people were born here?

343
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:27,550
How many people have finished
their last journey here?

344
00:15:27,550 --> 00:15:28,600
How many late nights

345
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,260
were the lights still on here?

346
00:15:30,510 --> 00:15:32,030
Today, it's coming to an end.

347
00:15:32,030 --> 00:15:33,320
How do you feel?

348
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:34,910
Do you have anything to say to these

349
00:15:34,910 --> 00:15:36,600
old neighbors who rushed here?

350
00:15:36,110 --> 00:15:41,410
[Filming]

351
00:15:36,870 --> 00:15:37,960
First of all,

352
00:15:39,030 --> 00:15:40,440
I support all the decisions

353
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,790
made by the responsible authorities.

354
00:15:41,790 --> 00:15:44,790
Xiaoximen Hospital indeed
has its own difficulties.

355
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:48,290
Its conditions are not as good as
those big hospitals,

356
00:15:48,290 --> 00:15:51,780
[Filming]

357
00:15:48,910 --> 00:15:50,960
but for everyone, you can see a doctor

358
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:52,200
just by walking a few steps.

359
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:54,360
You don't have to line up in the dark
to register.

360
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:56,960
It's the first place nearby residents
think of

361
00:15:57,150 --> 00:15:58,480
when they get sick.

362
00:15:59,240 --> 00:15:59,790
That's right.

363
00:15:59,790 --> 00:16:00,910
Right.

364
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:05,270
Xiaoximen Hospital indeed can't compare
with big hospitals,

365
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:06,240
but it allows

366
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:08,790
the surrounding residents to see a doctor.

367
00:16:06,810 --> 00:16:15,710
[Filming]

368
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,080
It gives them a choice.

369
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:13,480
You can't leave the common people with

370
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,390
no options when they need to
see a doctor, right?

371
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:15,480
-Yeah.
-Xiao Long.

372
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:16,870
For what you just said,

373
00:16:16,870 --> 00:16:18,440
I have to give you a thumbs up.

374
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:19,840
I trust Xiaoximen Hospital.

375
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:21,240
Let me say a few words too.

376
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:23,240
When people get old,

377
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:25,040
[Filming]

378
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,910
they have a lot of troubles and illnesses.

379
00:16:24,910 --> 00:16:25,630
Right?

380
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,150
In the past,

381
00:16:27,150 --> 00:16:29,270
when we had any illnesses or diseases,

382
00:16:29,270 --> 00:16:30,510
we went to Xiaoximen Hospital.

383
00:16:30,510 --> 00:16:31,870
Xiaoximen Hospital didn't despise us.

384
00:16:31,870 --> 00:16:32,550
Right?

385
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,200
Right.

386
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,030
But now,

387
00:16:34,030 --> 00:16:35,720
you are closing Xiaoximen Hospital.

388
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:36,840
Then when we get sick in the future,

389
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:37,720
who are we going to look for?

390
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:38,390
Yes.

391
00:16:38,390 --> 00:16:39,080
Right?

392
00:16:41,030 --> 00:16:42,960
This brother is right.

393
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:43,600
Right.

394
00:16:44,510 --> 00:16:46,390
Although Xiaoximen Hospital is small,

395
00:16:46,390 --> 00:16:47,960
it has made a lot of contributions.

396
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:50,790
[Filming]

397
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:48,440
Right.

398
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,120
Take me for example.

399
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:52,720
I have this complicated medical condition

400
00:16:52,750 --> 00:16:54,240
and wasn't it cured

401
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:54,960
by that doctor surnamed Liu

402
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:55,870
in no time?

403
00:16:56,030 --> 00:16:57,120
Yes, exactly.

404
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:59,000
Xiaoximen Hospital may be average,

405
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,670
but for us common people,

406
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:01,690
it's enough.

407
00:17:01,790 --> 00:17:03,080
Right.

408
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,400
What is good?

409
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:09,020
[Filming]

410
00:17:04,550 --> 00:17:05,960
Suitable is good.

411
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:06,960
Am I right, everyone?

412
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,240
Right.

413
00:17:08,510 --> 00:17:09,109
Right.

414
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:11,030
Xiaoximen Hospital can't be closed.

415
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,630
If it's closed,
where will we go to see a doctor?

416
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:31,960
Hello.

417
00:17:32,030 --> 00:17:33,160
Hello, Zhengliang.

418
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:33,880
Brother,

419
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:35,000
you finally answered the phone.

420
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:35,590
Look at how many calls

421
00:17:35,590 --> 00:17:36,640
I made to you.

422
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:37,880
I even thought

423
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:39,070
you were kidnapped.

424
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:40,720
Kidnapped?

425
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:42,920
I'm not a kid anymore.

426
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:45,440
I won't get lost. Don't worry.

427
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,480
Who says?

428
00:17:47,830 --> 00:17:48,920
Do you remember

429
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,530
when we were in high school,

430
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:52,200
you ran away from home

431
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:54,200
and actually got lost?

432
00:17:54,830 --> 00:17:55,590
In the end, I remember

433
00:17:55,590 --> 00:17:56,640
it was the police

434
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:57,840
who found you, right?

435
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:58,880
At that time,

436
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,000
you were already 18

437
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,400
and officially an adult.

438
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,920
Why talk about that year?

439
00:18:03,640 --> 00:18:04,440
Why don't you talk about

440
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:06,310
getting beaten up when you were a kid?

441
00:18:06,310 --> 00:18:09,170
Not talking about it doesn't mean
I don't remember.

442
00:18:12,830 --> 00:18:14,030
When will you be back?

443
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,920
In a little while.

444
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,180
I want to hide for a bit.

445
00:18:22,070 --> 00:18:22,960
I understand.

446
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:24,220
I totally understand.

447
00:18:25,030 --> 00:18:26,760
I've thought about hiding too.

448
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,550
Did you succeed?

449
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:30,880
What do you think?

450
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:33,590
Let me tell you something.

451
00:18:33,590 --> 00:18:35,520
Sometimes the more you try to hide,

452
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:37,550
the less you can get away from it.

453
00:18:39,590 --> 00:18:40,790
Then what should I do?

454
00:18:40,830 --> 00:18:41,960
What can you do?

455
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:43,550
Just keep living.

456
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,120
Don't worry. I won't die.

457
00:18:49,310 --> 00:18:50,970
I'll wait for you to come back.

458
00:18:57,070 --> 00:18:57,790
If my phone

459
00:18:57,790 --> 00:18:59,160
loses signal later

460
00:19:00,070 --> 00:19:01,330
and you can't reach me,

461
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,310
help me tell my parents

462
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:06,590
that I'm safe.

463
00:19:06,790 --> 00:19:08,160
Wait, where are you that

464
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,220
there's no signal?

465
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,510
A good place.

466
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:16,960
What good place?

467
00:19:17,310 --> 00:19:18,170
I'm hanging up.

468
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:34,640
Chen Junnan!

469
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:40,750
Chen Junnan!

470
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:41,880
Zhang Hao!

471
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:43,270
You—

472
00:19:44,030 --> 00:19:44,960
What's with this outfit?

473
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,000
Come, give it to me.

474
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:46,680
The luggage.

475
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:47,680
Hello, hello, hello.

476
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,880
Hello, hello, hello.

477
00:19:49,790 --> 00:19:50,510
You—

478
00:19:50,750 --> 00:19:52,030
You look completely different.

479
00:19:52,030 --> 00:19:52,680
Right?

480
00:19:54,510 --> 00:19:55,710
You came by yourself?

481
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,180
Yeah, I came by myself.

482
00:19:57,880 --> 00:19:59,280
I wasn't bragging, was I?

483
00:19:59,830 --> 00:20:01,550
Snowfields, big forest.

484
00:20:01,550 --> 00:20:02,310
See that?

485
00:20:02,750 --> 00:20:03,550
Isn't it cool?

486
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,640
This is great.

487
00:20:10,110 --> 00:20:12,160
This is the life we yearn for.

488
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:30,310
Just this outer layer.

489
00:20:30,310 --> 00:20:31,310
Didn't you say you didn't want it?

490
00:20:31,310 --> 00:20:32,680
You'll peel it bald.

491
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:34,320
What are you doing with this?

492
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:37,810
I have to do it like this.

493
00:20:38,350 --> 00:20:39,030
Right?

494
00:20:39,310 --> 00:20:39,910
Like this.

495
00:20:40,550 --> 00:20:41,240
Pound it.

496
00:20:41,830 --> 00:20:42,440
Like this?

497
00:20:43,270 --> 00:20:44,830
This is super simple.

498
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:46,780
Not as complicated as dumplings.

499
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:48,000
Just like this,

500
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,530
your hand curves like this.

501
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,260
How many have you made?

502
00:20:52,310 --> 00:20:53,310
How many people?

503
00:20:53,790 --> 00:20:54,640
Four people.

504
00:21:02,680 --> 00:21:03,590
See? Done.

505
00:21:06,550 --> 00:21:09,350
Dip it in water
and wipe the edge of the plate clean.

506
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:10,030
Okay.

507
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,200
When I'm home,

508
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,200
I make the cold dishes.

509
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,310
Coming.

510
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,680
That's incredible.

511
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,030
Zhengliang, I...

512
00:21:23,030 --> 00:21:24,480
I thought you meant treating us to dinner

513
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:25,200
at a restaurant.

514
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,000
I didn't expect it to be at home.

515
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,590
I didn't know you could cook.

516
00:21:27,590 --> 00:21:28,400
Ai Chen made it.

517
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,730
No, we made it together.

518
00:21:29,750 --> 00:21:31,240
-You're amazing.
-Never underestimate

519
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,400
the hands-on skills

520
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,160
of an excellent surgeon.

521
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:33,960
Absolutely.

522
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:36,420
Especially one who's lived
alone for years.

523
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:38,590
I almost forgot.

524
00:21:38,590 --> 00:21:39,830
I—I know what you want.

525
00:21:39,830 --> 00:21:41,920
-What are you getting?
-No, don't. It's enough.

526
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:44,030
-Six dishes for four. Enough.
-Enough, this is plenty.

527
00:21:44,030 --> 00:21:44,510
Here.

528
00:21:44,510 --> 00:21:44,880
It's enough.

529
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:45,270
For the trash.

530
00:21:45,270 --> 00:21:46,160
I know it's enough.

531
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:47,480
There's plenty of this too. Come on.

532
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,270
This...

533
00:21:48,270 --> 00:21:50,550
Are my eyes playing tricks on me?

534
00:21:51,030 --> 00:21:52,680
Wait, didn't you say you don't drink?

535
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,640
Just because I don't drink

536
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:55,070
doesn't mean you can't.

537
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:56,590
Zhengliang,

538
00:21:56,590 --> 00:21:57,200
what you just said

539
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,880
really warms my heart.

540
00:21:58,960 --> 00:21:59,680
Zhengliang...

541
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:00,270
Come on.

542
00:22:00,270 --> 00:22:01,400
You're good to go now.

543
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:02,880
Come on, let's start!

544
00:22:03,750 --> 00:22:04,510
Well,

545
00:22:04,510 --> 00:22:05,720
before we get started,

546
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,000
I'd like to say a few words.

547
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:07,720
Is that okay?

548
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:08,550
S-Sure.

549
00:22:08,550 --> 00:22:10,030
Yes, absolutely.

550
00:22:10,510 --> 00:22:11,510
Here's the thing.

551
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:13,290
The reason for this meal

552
00:22:13,790 --> 00:22:14,830
is that I wanted

553
00:22:15,110 --> 00:22:16,110
to invite you all,

554
00:22:16,230 --> 00:22:17,790
along with Chen Junnan

555
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,410
and my brother Zhengguang.

556
00:22:19,550 --> 00:22:21,000
I just wanted to thank you all

557
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,720
for taking care of me

558
00:22:22,830 --> 00:22:23,920
during this time.

559
00:22:25,350 --> 00:22:26,270
But then...

560
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,880
Zhengguang went to Beijing,

561
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:30,640
and Chen Junnan isn't here either.

562
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:32,240
But I said I'd treat you,

563
00:22:32,310 --> 00:22:34,510
-so I had to, right?
-Of course.

564
00:22:36,030 --> 00:22:37,030
So anyway—

565
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,110
W-Well, eat up and drink up!

566
00:22:46,110 --> 00:22:46,920
All right.

567
00:22:47,640 --> 00:22:48,440
Great!

568
00:22:48,480 --> 00:22:49,510
Cheers! Cheers!

569
00:22:52,030 --> 00:22:53,310
Who is it at this hour?

570
00:22:54,110 --> 00:22:54,920
Let's have a drink first.

571
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:55,980
Let's drink first.

572
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:59,550
Jin, Secretary Lyu,

573
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:00,570
why are you here?

574
00:23:01,070 --> 00:23:02,750
We heard Chief Physician Liu was treating,

575
00:23:02,750 --> 00:23:04,030
and we thought it was quite rare,

576
00:23:04,030 --> 00:23:05,240
so we came uninvited.

577
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:06,850
Hope you don't mind.

578
00:23:07,310 --> 00:23:08,110
Who told you

579
00:23:08,110 --> 00:23:09,110
I was treating?

580
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:11,000
Huang.

581
00:23:12,110 --> 00:23:12,770
You said it?

582
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,680
I... I came with him.

583
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:18,920
Yes.

584
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:19,920
I came with him.

585
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,070
We brought some fruit.

586
00:23:21,070 --> 00:23:21,920
It's all from before,

587
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,920
gifts people sent to the president.

588
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:25,920
Hey, even if you're coughing,

589
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:28,180
they were still gifts from someone else.

590
00:23:28,830 --> 00:23:30,750
Don't worry. I picked them out.

591
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:32,550
All good fruit, nothing rotten.

592
00:23:33,640 --> 00:23:34,510
Chief Physician Liu, here's the thing.

593
00:23:34,510 --> 00:23:36,440
Everyone's been
having a rough time lately.

594
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:38,040
I'm sure you can understand.

595
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:40,240
Well, um...

596
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:40,880
Come—come in.

597
00:23:40,880 --> 00:23:42,030
It's freezing outside.

598
00:23:42,030 --> 00:23:43,560
Since you're already here.

599
00:23:44,270 --> 00:23:45,000
Should we change our shoes?

600
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:45,830
It's fine, no need.

601
00:23:45,830 --> 00:23:46,400
Come in.

602
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:49,720
There might not be enough food.

603
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:50,750
I'll whip up two more dishes.

604
00:23:50,750 --> 00:23:51,550
No need.

605
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:52,830
Enough, enough, enough.

606
00:23:52,830 --> 00:23:53,750
Six dishes for six people.

607
00:23:53,750 --> 00:23:54,550
It's more than enough.

608
00:23:54,550 --> 00:23:55,310
It's enough. It's enough.

609
00:23:55,310 --> 00:23:55,720
Alright then.

610
00:23:55,720 --> 00:23:56,920
I... I don't eat much.

611
00:23:57,270 --> 00:23:58,350
Then let's eat while it's hot.

612
00:23:58,350 --> 00:23:58,750
Okay.

613
00:23:58,750 --> 00:23:59,680
Let's start over.

614
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:00,030
Let's start.

615
00:24:00,030 --> 00:24:00,510
Okay.

616
00:24:00,510 --> 00:24:02,160
What about Chen Junnan?

617
00:24:02,270 --> 00:24:03,730
Aren't you a group of four?

618
00:24:05,790 --> 00:24:07,650
He went off to cultivate himself.

619
00:24:09,070 --> 00:24:10,110
Cultivation is good.

620
00:24:10,110 --> 00:24:12,440
There are inevitably some hurdles in life.

621
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:13,160
Exactly.

622
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:14,720
Then let's drink to cultivation.

623
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:15,200
How about it?

624
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:16,230
Come on, cheers!

625
00:24:16,230 --> 00:24:17,920
To cultivation! Come on!

626
00:24:34,550 --> 00:24:35,790
I Heard Chief Physician Liu's
hosting dinner.

627
00:24:35,790 --> 00:24:36,790
I was so curious.

628
00:24:36,790 --> 00:24:37,440
So I came uninvited.

629
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:38,350
Sorry. I'm sorry.

630
00:24:38,350 --> 00:24:39,550
Chief Physician Liu.

631
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:41,200
You didn't even invite us to your treat.

632
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:42,270
That's not cool at all.

633
00:24:42,270 --> 00:24:44,440
Liu, I even made two dishes.

634
00:24:44,640 --> 00:24:46,370
And brought you some pastries.

635
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:48,080
No, no, no. Wait a minute.

636
00:24:48,110 --> 00:24:49,400
Who did you hear it from?

637
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:50,720
I heard it from him.

638
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:55,270
Should we change our shoes?

639
00:24:55,270 --> 00:24:56,550
Let's talk inside.

640
00:24:56,830 --> 00:24:57,480
It's cold outside.

641
00:24:57,480 --> 00:24:58,790
I heard it from them!

642
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:01,160
I heard it from them!

643
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:03,310
I knew you two would show up.

644
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:04,920
Everyone's curious, right?

645
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:05,310
Yes.

646
00:25:05,310 --> 00:25:07,070
Well, didn't the hospital close down?

647
00:25:07,070 --> 00:25:08,000
We have no work.

648
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:09,720
We're idle anyway.

649
00:25:10,030 --> 00:25:11,160
Wait, one question.

650
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:12,750
Who else did you tell?

651
00:25:13,310 --> 00:25:14,070
No one.

652
00:25:14,110 --> 00:25:14,750
No one.

653
00:25:14,750 --> 00:25:16,510
I was just going to have dinner
with these two.

654
00:25:16,510 --> 00:25:18,310
Otherwise, I wouldn't have even told them.

655
00:25:18,310 --> 00:25:19,110
Well...

656
00:25:19,110 --> 00:25:20,400
Basically, almost.

657
00:25:20,720 --> 00:25:21,480
Not basically.

658
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:22,070
Absolutely no one else.

659
00:25:22,070 --> 00:25:23,330
There should be no one.

660
00:25:23,920 --> 00:25:25,450
There's no more room to sit.

661
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:26,720
Let's squeeze in.

662
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:28,440
If anyone else comes,

663
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:29,400
we'll have to sit on each other's laps.

664
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:30,460
Take off your coat.

665
00:25:42,510 --> 00:25:43,570
Take off your coat.

666
00:25:49,030 --> 00:25:49,960
There's more?

667
00:25:50,790 --> 00:25:51,920
Why didn't you invite

668
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:52,880
the whole hospital?

669
00:25:52,880 --> 00:25:53,750
We really have to sit
on each other's laps.

670
00:25:53,750 --> 00:25:54,590
Was it you, bro?

671
00:25:54,590 --> 00:25:55,550
What's going on?

672
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:57,200
No, I-I'm tight-lipped.

673
00:25:57,590 --> 00:25:59,310
You're tight-lipped?
Yet someone's knocking.

674
00:25:59,310 --> 00:25:59,970
I didn't...

675
00:26:36,310 --> 00:26:37,030
You do it.

676
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:40,030
Welcome!

677
00:26:40,480 --> 00:26:41,940
Welcome, President Long!

678
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:54,750
Do you think Director Yan

679
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:56,070
thinks that

680
00:26:56,070 --> 00:26:59,310
since Xiaoximen is disbanded,

681
00:26:59,310 --> 00:27:01,270
we should all be at home

682
00:27:01,270 --> 00:27:02,680
crying our eyes out?

683
00:27:04,030 --> 00:27:05,070
We won't do that!

684
00:27:05,070 --> 00:27:05,750
Right!

685
00:27:05,750 --> 00:27:07,110
We've worked hard for most of our lives.

686
00:27:07,110 --> 00:27:09,270
We finally have some time

687
00:27:09,270 --> 00:27:10,750
to get a good rest at home.

688
00:27:10,750 --> 00:27:11,550
Isn't that nice?

689
00:27:11,550 --> 00:27:12,350
Right.

690
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:13,880
I don't want to rest.

691
00:27:14,030 --> 00:27:15,920
I don't know what to do when I'm free.

692
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:17,070
Ask Ai Chen.

693
00:27:17,640 --> 00:27:18,480
Me?

694
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:20,960
Do whatever you want.

695
00:27:21,240 --> 00:27:22,110
He is him. I am me.

696
00:27:22,110 --> 00:27:24,170
I've never told you what to do, right?

697
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:25,680
Right, well said.

698
00:27:26,640 --> 00:27:27,270
People

699
00:27:27,270 --> 00:27:29,070
shouldn't always think about work.

700
00:27:29,070 --> 00:27:31,000
Whether you're busy or not,

701
00:27:31,440 --> 00:27:33,300
you have to know how to enjoy life.

702
00:27:33,590 --> 00:27:34,400
Right.

703
00:27:38,070 --> 00:27:42,240
You once told me

704
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:43,440
What a voice.

705
00:27:43,440 --> 00:27:47,830
that meeting is a song.

706
00:27:49,480 --> 00:27:55,240
Eyes are the sea of spring.

707
00:27:55,480 --> 00:28:00,350
Youth is a green river.

708
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:06,070
Meeting is a song.

709
00:28:06,240 --> 00:28:11,030
Walking together, you and me.

710
00:28:10,730 --> 00:28:11,740
Pitch perfect!

711
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:17,240
The heart is a young sun,

712
00:28:17,350 --> 00:28:22,400
sincere and lively.

713
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:27,960
Meeting is a song.

714
00:28:28,070 --> 00:28:32,830
Walking together, you and me.

715
00:28:33,350 --> 00:28:38,310
The heart is a young sun,

716
00:28:38,510 --> 00:28:43,200
sincere and lively.

717
00:28:45,920 --> 00:28:47,310
Great! Let's drink!

718
00:28:47,480 --> 00:28:49,160
That song deserves a toast! Come on!

719
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:50,440
Have to drink to that!

720
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:51,030
You sang so well!

721
00:28:51,030 --> 00:28:51,720
Come on!

722
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:53,250
Someone forgot the lyrics.

723
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:54,720
Someone forgot the lyrics.

724
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:55,550
Who forgot the lyrics?

725
00:28:55,550 --> 00:28:57,610
That was the most in-sync we've been.

726
00:28:57,920 --> 00:28:58,720
Dr. Liu.

727
00:28:59,160 --> 00:28:59,960
Zhengliang.

728
00:29:00,590 --> 00:29:01,270
Here, drink this.

729
00:29:01,270 --> 00:29:02,730
Take a sip of this. Come on.

730
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:04,240
What? What?

731
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:05,440
Come on.

732
00:29:05,590 --> 00:29:06,480
What are you doing?

733
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:07,110
He's happy.

734
00:29:07,110 --> 00:29:08,350
No. You drink this.

735
00:29:08,550 --> 00:29:10,110
I saved it especially for you!

736
00:29:10,110 --> 00:29:11,590
-I saved it for you!
-He can't.

737
00:29:11,590 --> 00:29:12,480
Enough, Huang.

738
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:13,270
Here we go again.

739
00:29:13,270 --> 00:29:14,270
I don't drink.

740
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:15,880
Drink, drink.

741
00:29:15,880 --> 00:29:16,960
I can't drink.

742
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:18,240
Drink, just a little.

743
00:29:18,680 --> 00:29:19,480
I beg you.

744
00:29:19,480 --> 00:29:21,750
Red wine and baijiu aren't the same thing.

745
00:29:21,750 --> 00:29:23,270
Huang, you're drunk.

746
00:29:23,270 --> 00:29:23,920
It's all alcohol.

747
00:29:23,920 --> 00:29:25,350
What's the difference?

748
00:29:25,790 --> 00:29:27,790
This red wine looks like blood to me.

749
00:29:27,790 --> 00:29:29,250
Doesn't it make you dizzy?

750
00:29:29,270 --> 00:29:30,110
No.

751
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:33,000
Wine is wine. Blood is blood.

752
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,480
I'm a surgeon!

753
00:29:34,750 --> 00:29:36,680
That's tough, going into surgery.

754
00:29:37,640 --> 00:29:39,480
Thank you, Long!

755
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:41,030
That's enough.

756
00:29:41,030 --> 00:29:41,720
Thanks!

757
00:29:41,720 --> 00:29:42,510
Don't throw up on me.

758
00:29:42,510 --> 00:29:44,170
You're in internal medicine.

759
00:29:46,510 --> 00:29:48,240
You'll crush the president.

760
00:29:48,960 --> 00:29:50,620
-You two help.
-Go to the sofa.

761
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:52,720
Don't bump into anything.

762
00:29:52,720 --> 00:29:55,380
-Be gentle. Give him a hand.
-Careful, careful.

763
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:57,240
Slow down.

764
00:29:57,680 --> 00:30:00,340
He has to sleep it off every time
after drinking.

765
00:30:03,550 --> 00:30:04,680
Then we've got to do a toast.

766
00:30:04,680 --> 00:30:06,200
Come on!

767
00:30:06,790 --> 00:30:07,880
We've got to drink well!

768
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:08,510
Come on!

769
00:30:09,510 --> 00:30:10,910
Let him sleep for a while.

770
00:30:10,920 --> 00:30:11,790
He'll sober up soon.

771
00:30:11,790 --> 00:30:13,200
Come on, let's drink.

772
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:14,880
Are you okay, President?

773
00:30:15,310 --> 00:30:16,710
Didn't crush you, right?

774
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:20,310
Huang used to be a surgeon.

775
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:27,000
Around 1999, I think.

776
00:30:29,030 --> 00:30:30,480
He was young back then,

777
00:30:30,920 --> 00:30:32,310
just around thirty.

778
00:30:34,070 --> 00:30:35,880
We both worked at the First Mine Hospital.

779
00:30:35,880 --> 00:30:38,540
I was the director
of the emergency department.

780
00:30:39,070 --> 00:30:41,790
He was my best

781
00:30:42,510 --> 00:30:44,110
surgical emergency doctor.

782
00:30:47,110 --> 00:30:48,000
Once,

783
00:30:48,550 --> 00:30:50,350
there was a major mine accident.

784
00:30:51,110 --> 00:30:52,350
Huang spent

785
00:30:53,510 --> 00:30:54,310
several days

786
00:30:55,110 --> 00:30:58,310
rescuing the wounded.

787
00:31:00,110 --> 00:31:01,110
He treated over a dozen

788
00:31:01,110 --> 00:31:02,840
critically injured patients.

789
00:31:06,510 --> 00:31:07,770
None of them survived.

790
00:32:13,590 --> 00:32:15,000
I was in charge of

791
00:32:15,310 --> 00:32:16,570
directing the rescue.

792
00:32:17,030 --> 00:32:18,240
I couldn't feel

793
00:32:18,270 --> 00:32:20,720
their feelings on the front line.

794
00:32:21,720 --> 00:32:23,120
Later, Huang broke down.

795
00:32:24,510 --> 00:32:25,680
His spirit, emotions, and ideals

796
00:32:25,680 --> 00:32:26,640
were shattered.

797
00:32:29,510 --> 00:32:30,270
And he ended up with

798
00:32:30,270 --> 00:32:32,330
that awful condition—blood phobia.

799
00:32:49,550 --> 00:32:50,350
Later on,

800
00:32:52,510 --> 00:32:54,840
I was transferred to the Second Hospital.

801
00:32:55,880 --> 00:32:56,720
And Huang,

802
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:02,270
through his own hard work,

803
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:06,360
finally transferred from surgery
to internal medicine.

804
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:09,420
But nobody wanted him.

805
00:33:10,240 --> 00:33:11,200
Nobody paid him any mind.

806
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:12,730
I thought, what should I do?

807
00:33:14,310 --> 00:33:15,030
So I pulled some strings

808
00:33:15,030 --> 00:33:16,880
and got him into Xiaoximen.

809
00:33:17,200 --> 00:33:19,400
He's been here for almost twenty years.

810
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:25,800
Everyone at the hospital

811
00:33:26,030 --> 00:33:27,480
thinks Huang

812
00:33:28,790 --> 00:33:29,750
has given up,

813
00:33:30,960 --> 00:33:32,560
just coasting through life.

814
00:33:32,790 --> 00:33:33,830
Only I know

815
00:33:35,350 --> 00:33:37,080
that's not what he wants at all.

816
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:38,400
He doesn't want this.

817
00:33:41,750 --> 00:33:43,210
This isn't what he wanted.

818
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:54,550
Why did we become doctors?

819
00:33:56,480 --> 00:33:58,210
Have you ever thought about it?

820
00:33:59,720 --> 00:34:01,000
We study longer

821
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:02,160
than anyone else,

822
00:34:02,590 --> 00:34:03,480
work harder,

823
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:04,920
day and night,

824
00:34:05,030 --> 00:34:06,830
and still don't make much money.

825
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:09,150
You're so right.

826
00:34:10,070 --> 00:34:13,510
Doctors are practically
a high-risk profession now.

827
00:34:13,670 --> 00:34:15,360
If my dad hadn't gotten sick,

828
00:34:15,550 --> 00:34:17,480
I wouldn't have studied medicine.

829
00:34:18,070 --> 00:34:19,760
But once you become a doctor,

830
00:34:21,110 --> 00:34:21,960
you always feel

831
00:34:21,960 --> 00:34:23,560
there's something up ahead,

832
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:26,340
and you just want to run toward it,

833
00:34:26,840 --> 00:34:28,190
and chase it.

834
00:34:29,670 --> 00:34:30,510
But,

835
00:34:32,590 --> 00:34:34,070
how does that saying go?

836
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:35,630
Like feet without a bird,

837
00:34:35,630 --> 00:34:36,510
and then I just

838
00:34:36,840 --> 00:34:37,760
can't stop.

839
00:34:40,070 --> 00:34:41,510
Feet without a bird?

840
00:34:41,590 --> 00:34:42,719
A bird without feet.

841
00:34:50,710 --> 00:34:51,770
What are you doing?

842
00:34:52,030 --> 00:34:53,110
To our profession.

843
00:34:55,550 --> 00:34:56,150
Here.

844
00:34:56,190 --> 00:34:56,840
Here.

845
00:34:57,280 --> 00:34:57,920
To doctors!

846
00:34:57,920 --> 00:34:58,710
To doctors! Come on!

847
00:34:58,710 --> 00:34:59,510
To doctors!

848
00:35:01,510 --> 00:35:02,840
To all medical workers.

849
00:35:17,370 --> 00:35:20,520
♪ A soul that came to earth
amid the cries ♪

850
00:35:20,970 --> 00:35:24,140
♪ Welcome to this city of haste ♪

851
00:35:24,580 --> 00:35:26,940
♪ Grow taller, quick as you can ♪

852
00:35:27,240 --> 00:35:29,500
♪ Learn how to find your footing ♪

853
00:35:31,770 --> 00:35:35,140
♪ A soul who hid
among the lanes and alleys ♪

854
00:35:35,540 --> 00:35:38,810
♪ A single turn, and the lamp
at the door grows distant ♪

855
00:35:39,140 --> 00:35:41,530
♪ The ticket bears no way back ♪

856
00:35:41,820 --> 00:35:44,210
♪ How like life it is ♪

857
00:35:46,530 --> 00:35:48,890
♪ May every road you take be safe ♪

858
00:35:49,160 --> 00:35:53,270
♪ May the scenery stay simple
and carry you past regret ♪

859
00:35:53,810 --> 00:35:56,810
♪ Love deeply whatever comes to meet you ♪

860
00:35:57,400 --> 00:36:00,580
♪ And let those who leave be buried
under snow on the hills ♪

861
00:36:01,090 --> 00:36:03,510
♪ May you come home covered in dust ♪

862
00:36:03,910 --> 00:36:07,820
♪ Held by what you love
as you roam the world and return ♪

863
00:36:09,170 --> 00:36:13,430
♪ Saying the flowers
by the door are truly beautiful ♪

864
00:36:19,450 --> 00:36:22,690
♪ You'll pass through the seasons,
through dawn and dusk ♪

865
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:27,580
[Chen Junnan]

866
00:36:23,040 --> 00:36:26,230
♪ Hearing someone call your name,
again and again ♪

867
00:36:26,660 --> 00:36:28,970
♪ These ties may hurt a little ♪

868
00:36:29,550 --> 00:36:31,630
♪ Don't heal a broken heart ♪

869
00:36:34,020 --> 00:36:37,070
♪ It will bear witness
to the life you bravely lived ♪

870
00:36:37,550 --> 00:36:40,710
♪ To the beautiful souls you've loved ♪

871
00:36:41,210 --> 00:36:43,450
♪ To the address you call home ♪

872
00:36:43,930 --> 00:36:46,560
♪ In the little town
you've wandered through ♪

873
00:36:49,450 --> 00:36:51,630
♪ The wind in the city ♪

874
00:36:52,070 --> 00:36:54,810
♪ Blows through dreams
that flicker between light and dark ♪

875
00:36:55,690 --> 00:36:58,370
♪ Blows through one soul's radiance ♪

876
00:36:59,990 --> 00:37:02,520
♪ And all its weathered scars ♪

877
00:37:03,860 --> 00:37:06,170
♪ Blows through the depths of winter ♪

878
00:37:06,460 --> 00:37:09,340
♪ Stumbling along in the wind ♪

879
00:37:10,330 --> 00:37:12,900
♪ Flickering along in the wind ♪

880
00:37:14,550 --> 00:37:20,420
♪ Toward the crossroads
brimming with sunlight ♪

881
00:37:16,060 --> 00:37:23,710
[Registration]

882
00:37:23,710 --> 00:37:31,940
[The Return of the Condor Heroes]

883
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:27,280
♪ May every road you take be safe ♪

884
00:37:27,460 --> 00:37:31,480
♪ May the scenery stay simple
and carry you past regret ♪

885
00:37:32,160 --> 00:37:35,180
♪ Love deeply whatever comes to meet you ♪

886
00:37:35,490 --> 00:37:36,250
[Xinhua Dictionary]

887
00:37:35,620 --> 00:37:38,720
♪ And let those who leave be buried
under snow on the hills ♪

888
00:37:36,270 --> 00:37:39,310
[The Return of the Condor Heroes]

889
00:37:39,380 --> 00:37:41,820
♪ May you come home covered in dust ♪

890
00:37:42,090 --> 00:37:46,020
♪ Held by what you love
as you roam the world and return ♪

891
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:45,590
San.

892
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:47,110
Put this on,

893
00:37:47,190 --> 00:37:48,630
and the shelf will be full.

894
00:37:47,220 --> 00:37:51,450
♪ Saying she was so beautiful
in front of the door ♪

895
00:37:48,840 --> 00:37:50,880
I'll come look with you every day.

896
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:53,670
Once we've seen enough,
maybe we won't want to take it.

897
00:37:53,670 --> 00:37:54,920
Fight fire with fire.

898
00:37:57,150 --> 00:37:58,030
I really didn't expect

899
00:37:57,880 --> 00:38:00,030
[Linmon Express]

900
00:37:58,670 --> 00:38:00,480
you to help out last time.

901
00:38:00,590 --> 00:38:01,280
It was nothing.

902
00:38:01,280 --> 00:38:02,510
We happen to be short of hands here.

903
00:38:02,510 --> 00:38:05,170
The station manager said
you could come to talk.

904
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:06,190
Work hard.

905
00:38:05,550 --> 00:38:07,660
[Bulk Sorting Area]

906
00:38:07,840 --> 00:38:08,630
Come.

907
00:38:09,590 --> 00:38:10,400
Manager.

908
00:38:10,960 --> 00:38:12,230
I brought Zhengguang.

909
00:38:12,550 --> 00:38:14,880
Zhengguang, this is our station manager.

910
00:38:20,710 --> 00:38:21,640
Hello, Manager.

911
00:38:37,710 --> 00:38:38,970
Why are you still here?

912
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:39,800
You're awake.

913
00:38:42,710 --> 00:38:44,240
If I leave, what will you do?

914
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:47,760
Someone has to

915
00:38:47,760 --> 00:38:49,110
clean up this mess.

916
00:38:52,760 --> 00:38:53,550
Thank you.

917
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:10,880
Why are you staring at me?

918
00:39:23,670 --> 00:39:24,880
I want to treat you.

919
00:39:29,070 --> 00:39:30,320
You want to treat me?

920
00:39:38,190 --> 00:39:40,440
Yes, I'll treat your chionophobia.

921
00:39:44,400 --> 00:39:46,130
I have to make sure you can stay.

922
00:39:47,590 --> 00:39:49,710
Okay, thank you.

923
00:39:50,280 --> 00:39:51,030
But for my illness,

924
00:39:51,030 --> 00:39:51,800
I can only endure it.

925
00:39:51,800 --> 00:39:52,880
Endure it?

926
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:55,800
Aren't you avoiding the problem?

927
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:57,320
You're just like Huang.

928
00:39:57,590 --> 00:39:59,790
It's been over ten years for him, right?

929
00:40:01,360 --> 00:40:02,110
His hemophobia

930
00:40:02,110 --> 00:40:03,480
has never been cured.

931
00:40:05,630 --> 00:40:07,290
Just let me endure it with you,

932
00:40:07,320 --> 00:40:08,710
and hope every year

933
00:40:08,710 --> 00:40:09,920
that it won't snow.

934
00:40:14,710 --> 00:40:16,370
I'm not avoiding the problem.

935
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:18,150
I've seen many doctors

936
00:40:18,320 --> 00:40:19,440
and experts.

937
00:40:19,670 --> 00:40:22,670
-They all said...
-It depends on man's will, you know?

938
00:40:23,920 --> 00:40:25,480
You just need to promise me,

939
00:40:26,670 --> 00:40:28,600
and then we'll work on it together.

940
00:40:55,320 --> 00:40:55,920
Hello?

941
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:56,880
What are you doing?

942
00:40:56,880 --> 00:40:58,680
Why did it take so long to answer?

943
00:40:59,110 --> 00:41:00,280
I was sleeping.

944
00:41:00,960 --> 00:41:01,880
Get downstairs, quick.

945
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:02,590
Good news.

946
00:41:05,550 --> 00:41:06,670
Okay, wait for me.

947
00:41:22,630 --> 00:41:23,550
What are you doing?

948
00:41:23,550 --> 00:41:24,550
Scared?

949
00:41:25,510 --> 00:41:26,480
I'm treating you.

950
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:28,740
Treating? What kind of treating is this?

951
00:41:29,550 --> 00:41:31,410
This is called exposure therapy.

952
00:41:31,440 --> 00:41:32,840
Also known as flooding therapy!

953
00:41:32,840 --> 00:41:33,630
Scared?

954
00:41:33,630 --> 00:41:35,840
It puts you deep in your fear,

955
00:41:35,920 --> 00:41:36,880
and then after two or three times,

956
00:41:36,880 --> 00:41:39,480
once you're not scared anymore,
you're cured.

957
00:41:40,150 --> 00:41:41,150
If curing illnesses were this simple,

958
00:41:41,150 --> 00:41:42,410
there'd be no doctors.

959
00:41:42,550 --> 00:41:43,670
You're awesome!

960
00:41:44,230 --> 00:41:45,400
You held on!

961
00:41:46,480 --> 00:41:47,760
The inspiration came from

962
00:41:47,760 --> 00:41:48,840
us washing dishes.

963
00:41:51,110 --> 00:41:52,190
So when you said treating me,

964
00:41:52,190 --> 00:41:53,550
this is how you meant to do it?

965
00:41:53,550 --> 00:41:54,480
Great!

966
00:41:55,920 --> 00:41:56,840
All right, come down!

967
00:41:56,840 --> 00:41:57,590
Come down!

968
00:41:59,440 --> 00:42:00,630
Spread it evenly.

969
00:42:01,480 --> 00:42:02,940
All right, stop spraying!

970
00:42:04,880 --> 00:42:05,670
Done.

971
00:42:07,550 --> 00:42:08,950
Take a moment to recover.

972
00:42:09,190 --> 00:42:10,000
Wait for me!

973
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:10,670
Easy, Chen.

974
00:42:13,510 --> 00:42:14,320
How was it?

975
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:16,880
So realistic.

976
00:42:18,110 --> 00:42:18,960
How'd it feel?

977
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:20,190
What's there to feel?

978
00:42:20,190 --> 00:42:21,960
This is foam, not snow.

979
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:24,960
What do you mean? No—no feeling?

980
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,230
You have no imagination.

981
00:42:26,230 --> 00:42:27,830
Can't you imagine it's snow?

982
00:42:28,280 --> 00:42:29,190
You need to feel

983
00:42:29,190 --> 00:42:30,030
the chilly wind

984
00:42:30,030 --> 00:42:31,000
and the heavy snow.

985
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:31,710
I adjusted it for you.

986
00:42:31,710 --> 00:42:32,880
It's all heavy snow.

987
00:42:33,400 --> 00:42:35,030
I felt the chilly wind.

988
00:42:35,550 --> 00:42:36,400
But this...

989
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:37,550
foam is foam.

990
00:42:37,550 --> 00:42:38,440
It's not snow.

991
00:42:38,440 --> 00:42:39,280
How can I imagine it?

992
00:42:39,280 --> 00:42:40,400
I'm not a goldfish.

993
00:42:42,070 --> 00:42:43,760
Why are you so stubborn?

994
00:42:44,630 --> 00:42:46,890
You run away when you face difficulties.

995
00:42:47,190 --> 00:42:48,760
When dealing with your illness,

996
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:50,030
you need to show some willpower.

997
00:42:50,030 --> 00:42:50,840
You know?

998
00:42:51,400 --> 00:42:53,190
Come on, willpower?

999
00:42:53,710 --> 00:42:54,550
Easy for you to say.

1000
00:42:54,550 --> 00:42:55,550
Why don't you use your willpower

1001
00:42:55,550 --> 00:42:57,190
to cure your illiteracy?

1002
00:43:02,230 --> 00:43:03,290
Keep provoking me.

1003
00:43:03,670 --> 00:43:04,800
No violence, okay?

1004
00:43:05,110 --> 00:43:06,000
Neither of us can escape.

1005
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:06,760
You know?

1006
00:43:08,510 --> 00:43:10,040
I'll set an example for you.

1007
00:43:10,440 --> 00:43:11,550
I'll show you

1008
00:43:11,550 --> 00:43:13,000
how determined I am.
